      "message": "Surface sp/bc1 choice when a BIP-21 deep link carries both\n\nThe bitcoin: deep-link handler always auto-selected the silent-payment\naddress when a URI carried both endpoints, with no way to fall back to\nthe on-chain address. Match the QR-scan dual-endpoint behavior: push\nthe URI into the recipient picker so the dropdown surfaces both rows\nand the user explicitly picks privacy (sp) vs. compatibility (on-chain).\nSingle-endpoint URIs still auto-select as a chip.\n\nRegression-of: 8647e48b",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "aadaab35ff8d678410b47a050d5568c6aba22e8f",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/trees/aadaab35ff8d678410b47a050d5568c6aba22e8f"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/soapbox-pub/ditto/git/commits/0fa0d08d45ed0fab8c8ac146a0acd86a9cc0a2a7",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
