        "payload": "tree aadaab35ff8d678410b47a050d5568c6aba22e8f\nparent d1e6f57b6b4744d2db729009749a3005959e75ef\nauthor Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1780000489 -0500\ncommitter Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me> 1780000489 -0500\n\nSurface sp/bc1 choice when a BIP-21 deep link carries both\n\nThe bitcoin: deep-link handler always auto-selected the silent-payment\naddress when a URI carried both endpoints, with no way to fall back to\nthe on-chain address. Match the QR-scan dual-endpoint behavior: push\nthe URI into the recipient picker so the dropdown surfaces both rows\nand the user explicitly picks privacy (sp) vs. compatibility (on-chain).\nSingle-endpoint URIs still auto-select as a chip.\n\nRegression-of: 8647e48b\n",
